  "method": "Exact chance enumeration and adversarial two-player backward induction in synthetic final-epoch puzzles. 2-3 unknown bag tiles, known equal public initial scores 100, 1-2 usable disks per player, all canonical legal actions. Draw probabilities use the public remaining multiset; no future-order peeking. Each objective is solved separately, with a 100000-node cap; capped cases excluded from exact conclusions.",
  "caveats": [
    "Synthetic fully specified two-player endgames, not full-game Ra playing-strength evidence.",
    "Opponent scores are deliberately public and equal in these fixtures; no real hidden score is used.",
    "Policy regret is relative to the stated win or margin objective, not proof of an error in historical games.",
    "The current MCTS itself is not benchmarked here; its restricted candidate set and heuristic policy are audited."
